  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.AmusedAnswers": "[pg]You answer all her questions, somewhat amused at her [if (!helspawnchaste) {not-quite-}]innocent excitement. But, as you tell her, that's only the first fish. You bet there are plenty more in this river for you to catch. The young salamander nods and sits back down next to you, seeming determined to keep going."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.AnglingJoyAdvice": "[pg]You tell her how happy you were to show her the joys of angling, but point out that she should get those fish to her [if (isfeminine) {other }]mother before too long. Wouldn't want all her hard work to go to waste."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.ArrowRequestSmile": "[pg]You simply smile and tell her to get out an arrow. The salamander does so and then offers it to you, doubt clear on her face. However, this uncertainty soon changes into understanding when she sees you pull out the twine you brought along and start binding it to the arrow. When you're done, you have in essence a miniature harpoon, which you then hand back over to your daughter."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.ArrowSailsWater": "[pg]The arrow sails off into the water, and [helspawn] excitedly pulls it back in with the attached string, only to be disappointed by a clean arrowhead."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.AsksWhatNext": "[pg][say:Thanks, [Dad]. So, uh... What now?]"
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.AsksYourPlan": "whereupon [helspawn] turns to you and asks, [say:So, what'd you have in mind? I'm not quite sure what the bow is for...]"
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.DeclineReturnHome": "[pg]You would, but you've been out here for long enough that you'd like to get back. And you're not sure exactly how edible the result of Helia's cooking will be. [Helspawn] takes this completely in stride, simply smiling and waving as you start towards camp, your [legs] a bit stiff."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.DeterminedAgreement": "[pg]She [if (helspawnchaste) {accepts your words with quiet determination|nods along agitatedly}], and you can tell that she wants to try again as soon as possible, so you stop talking and let her do so. The next few shots go similarly, and though the salamander gets a bit frustrated, there's an undeniable aura of pure fun as the two of you learn how this works together."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.DinnerInvitation": "[pg]She nods and says, [say:Well, would you like to join us? We caught more than enough. Well, I can make sure Mom leaves you some.]"
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.EnthusiasmInfectious": "[pg]Your daughter's enthusiasm is infectious, so you hurry her over to the very edge of the river and explain what to do. She nods along, and before you're even through, nocks her arrow and takes aim. The expression on her face is completely focused, so you decide not to interfere, instead watching as she shifts slightly to the right, waits a breath, and then looses her shot."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.ExcitedCatchBoast": "[pg][say:I got [if (helspawnchaste) {it, [Dad]|you, fucker}]! Did you see? How big do you think it is? Is it good to eat?]"
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.FashionFishingRod": "You'll need to fashion some sort of fishing rod, but you think you'll be able to with the things you have on hand. You ask [Helspawn] to fetch some wood from your reserves while you get to work on a nail. With some effort, you manage to bend it into a rough hook shape, and your daughter returns just as you're attaching it to a spare bit of twine."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.FirstCastLands": "[pg]Her first cast sails true over the waters, landing in the river with a little \"plop\". It was a good cast, as far as you can tell, so you make sure to let her know."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.FishStruckVictory": "[pg]And finally, through failure after failure, [helspawn] hits a fish cleanly in the side. A victorious whoop resounds off the riverbanks, [if (helspawnchaste) {before your daughter remembers herself|your daughter throwing her arms up in the air triumphantly}]. You celebrate her success, but she's quick to get back to it, a spark now lit in her eyes. You're right there at her side as she shoots again and again, giggling and grumbling as fit."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.FishingPlanIdea": "You have an excellent idea, one that should serve for both [timeofday] entertainment and [if (hours < 9) {breakfast|[if (hours < 14) {lunch|dinner}]}], so you stride right up to [helspawn] and tell her your plan--namely, that you'd like to fish with her."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.FourFishCatch": "[pg]All in all, the two of you manage to catch four fish that look like decent eating. By the end, [helspawn] starts to look a little tired, but that's pretty understandable, as judging by the sky, you've been out here for longer than you thought. You put your hand on her shoulder and tell her that it's about time to head in."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.GracefulFishArc": "[pg][Helspawn] pulls the fish in in a graceful arc that almost ends smack-dab in your face. Luckily, you dodge in time, but before you can comment on this, your daughter is letting out a gleeful shout, holding the fish up above her head."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.GratefulSmileReply": "[pg]She smiles in response and says, [say:[if (helspawnchaste) {Thank you, [Dad].|That was great, [Daddy]!}] I had a lot more fun than I thought I would.]"
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.HookSettingLesson": "[pg]You quickly inform her of how to set a hook, and she jerks the pole back just like you tell her to. At your direction, she begins fighting the fish, readily eating up all of your instructions. The gleam in her eyes is a sight to see, and you're even a bit surprised when the splash of something breaking the water draws your attention."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.LumberChoicePraise": "[pg]She's picked out a nice, slender piece of lumber, and you compliment her choice. The salamander [if (helspawnchaste) {blushes and mumbles out a thanks, and|just giggles and gives you an amused look, so}] you get to working on the wood. It doesn't take too long before you've got a proper pole on your hands, so you affix your line to it and then hold it up to admire your work."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.MissDisheartened": "[pg][say:I'm pretty sure that was dead on...] she says, clearly a bit disheartened. You explain to her that there's a lot of things different from normal archery here--the additional weight of the line, the water's distortion, and the additional resistance from passing through a liquid would all make it a lot harder to hit a target.{0}."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.PanickedShout": "[pg][say:Gah!] she shouts. [say:Wh-What do I do?]"
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.PeacefulRhythm": "[pg]You fall into a steady, peaceful rhythm. [if (helspawnchaste) {Neither you nor your daughter has any desire to disturb the serenity of the riverside|Your daughter is surprisingly quiet, seeming to be refreshingly content to just sit still and take in the atmosphere}]. You pass the rod back and forth in turns, though even when it's not in your hands, something about the way [helspawn] gets completely into it makes you feel like you're still behind the wheel."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.PerceptiveSmile": "[pg][say:[if (helspawnchaste) {I think I see what you're going for. It seems like it might be difficult, but I'd love to give it a shot.|So I just shoot them? That's great, why didn't you tell me!}]] [Helspawn] flashes you a [if (helspawnchaste) {slight smile|huge grin}]. [say:I'm ready to get started whenever you are.]"
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.RaisesHandUnsure": "[pg][say:Oh, but I don't really know how to use it,] she says, holding up a hand."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.RiverSpotDoubts": "[pg]You're not sure if the nearby river is the most ideal spot, but it should do well enough for your purposes. After all, this is more about the experience than actually getting food, though you do hope there'll be enough excitement to entertain your daughter. [if (helspawnchaste) {However, you realize that that probably won't be an issue. The glitter in [helspawn]'s [helspawneyes] eyes makes it clear that she's just as eager to get started as you|But thankfully, you think things will be just fine. Despite her earlier aloof attitude, you can tell that she's starting to warm up to the idea}]."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.RodImpressedReaction": "[pg][Helspawn] seems [if (helspawnchaste) {surprisingly impressed at the finished fishing rod, given how simple it is|a bit unimpressed with the finished work, but she takes your hand all the same}], and the two of you set off out of camp. On the way, you make sure to dig up some worms for bait."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.SecondIdeaStrikes": "But just as you're considering how you'd go about making a rod, a second great idea strikes you. You retrieve a length of string and ask your daughter to go get her bow. She looks a bit confused, but does so anyway, and you take the opportunity to fetch some spare twine. When she returns, you beckon her over and head off out of camp."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.SortGearFirst": "[pg]Well, if she's on board, you suppose that the first thing that needs sorting is equipment. "
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.SuddenTug": "[pg]And before you know it, a tug almost yanks the rod right out of her hands."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.SuitableStoneFound": "and you look about for a moment before spotting a suitable stone. It's wide, flat, and positioned close enough to the water that you should be able to use it. You wave the young salamander over and [if (singleleg) {lower yourself onto the rock|take a seat}], patting the spot next to you. [Helspawn] doesn't hesitate, and you offer her the rod as soon as she joins you."
  "Scenes.Helspawnscene.HelspawnFishing.TimeToWait": "[pg]You tell the salamander that now it's time to wait. She looks a bit [if (helspawnchaste) {confused|crestfallen}], so you explain that it could take some time to get a bite. Fishing is all about patience. At this word, she [if (helspawnchaste) {nods firmly and turns her attention back to the line|almost flinches, but manages to restrain herself}]. The line bobs in the water, and silence reigns."
